WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.914
"Side Effects of Metformin
as a Life-Extension Drug"

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.240
The apparent
reductions in mortality

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.680
from all causes put together

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.560
and diseases of aging
associated with metformin use

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.540
suggest that the drug metformin

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.520
could be extending
life and healthspans

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.100
by acting as a geroprotective,

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.080
or anti-aging, agent.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.300
What might the downsides be?

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.760
Gastrointestinal side-effects,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.900
such as flatulence,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.820
indigestion,
and abdominal discomfort,

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.780
are relatively common.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.060
More than half
starting metformin

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.620
report diarrhea, for example,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.840
and a quarter experience
nausea or vomiting.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.560
About 10 percent
unknowingly taking the placebo

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.120
report similar symptoms, though;

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.860
so, the actual
proportion of people

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.900
suffering such symptoms
due to the drug

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.480
is probably more like 1 in 3.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.100
Most of these effects
tend to be transient, though,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.040
and can be minimized
by taking metformin with food

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.320
and starting
at a suboptimal dose,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.060
increasing gradually to target

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.320
over a period of weeks.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.440
Once-a-day
extended-release versions

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.240
also tend to be more tolerable.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.360
The most dreaded
side effect, though,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.580
is lactic acidosis,

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.520
the potentially fatal buildup
of acid in the blood.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.580
I mean,
poisoning of the mitochondria

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.200
is kind of the whole point.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.360
That's what activates AMPK,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.840
but it's supposed to be a mild
mitochondrial poison,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.320
but sometimes it evidently
poisons a bit too much.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:29.880
Thankfully,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.100
metformin-induced
lactic acidosis

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.260
is extremely rare.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.920
It has a fatality rate
of 50 percent

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.020
but only occurs
at a rate of about

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.260
0.03 cases
per thousand patient-years.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.840
That means
taking metformin for a year

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.640
only has about a 1 in 67,000
chance of killing you.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.000
Lactic acidosis
is primarily caused

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.880
by insufficient metformin
clearance by the kidneys;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.920
so, risk can be minimized by,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:01:59.400
for example,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.320
temporarily stopping the drug

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.000
while undergoing procedures

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.620
that put the kidneys at risk,

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.400
such as major surgery
or intravenous contrast dyes

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.080
used for certain
imaging procedures.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.900
Those with
mild to moderate kidney disease

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.580
can still benefit from metformin

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.080
at an adjusted dose.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.120
Elderly individuals

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.580
should have their
kidney function tested

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.460
before starting metformin,
and regularly monitored.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.800
Excess alcohol consumption

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.480
is also believed
to increase the risk

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.880
of fatal metformin-induced
lactic acidosis.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.300
One of the more
insidious side effects

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.740
is B12 deficiency,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.240
vitamin B12 deficiency,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.980
affecting as many
as one in three

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.480
long-term metformin users,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.540
but can start
as early as a few months.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.980
The mechanism is still unclear,

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.880
but routine monitoring of B12
status has been recommended,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.760
and B12 supplementation
has been suggested.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.880
Another adverse consequence
of metformin

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.580
is less side effect
than main effect.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.300
Remember how metformin
is a mild mitochondrial poison?

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.760
The way metformin boosts AMPK

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.340
is by impairing our body's
ability to produce energy.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.640
What might that mean
for athletic performance?

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.760
Healthy men and women
were found to suffer

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.760
a significant decline
in peak aerobic capacity

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.640
after only about
a week on metformin.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.940
The average hit was only
three percent, though,

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.700
which could be meaningful
for an elite athlete

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.920
but would be unlikely to impede

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.360
recreational physical activity.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.900
However, some individuals
lost as much as 10 percent,

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.300
which could
be noticeably fatiguing.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.700
Note these detriments
were only found

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.220
at or near maximal workloads,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.600
and so, most active individuals

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.120
would be unlikely
to experience an impairment

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.320
in routine activity.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.180
Over the long term, though,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.000
metformin may undercut
physical fitness.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.760
Older adults were randomized

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.980
to 12 weeks
of supervised aerobic exercise

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.780
on or off metformin.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.840
They trained for 45 minutes
three times a week

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.520
on a treadmill,
bike, or elliptical,

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.260
ramping up to a vigorous target

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.360
of 85 percent
of their maximal heart rate.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.020
Unfortunately, metformin
attenuated the improvement

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.660
in physiological function
after exercise training.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.420
Cardiovascular fitness
is so important;

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:18.060
yet, after three months,
metformin cut their improvement

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:21.600
in cardiorespiratory fitness
in half compared to placebo,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.780
though this didn't reach
statistical significance.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.640
Metformin did, however,

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.380
significantly
blunt their improvement

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.360
in whole-body
insulin sensitivity

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.120
which normally improves
with physical activity.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.600
Aerobic exercise, (or "cardio")

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.720
is critical for maintaining
cardiovascular fitness,

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.520
whereas resistance exercise

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.260
(also known
as strength training,

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.700
for example,
with weights or bands)

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.460
is essential for maintaining
muscle mass as we age.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.780
In 2019,

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.300
the so-called MASTERS trial
was published,

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:54.600
investigating what metformin
might do to muscle gains,

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.240
and, the title of the paper
gives it away:

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.180
"Metformin blunts
muscle hypertrophy

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.280
in response to progressive
resistance exercise training

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.480
in older adults."

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.020
After 14 weeks of progressive
resistance training,

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.580
men and women
in the placebo group

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.680
accrued significant
lean body mass,

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.440
but those randomized
to the metformin group did not.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.840
For example,
about a four percent gain

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.940
in thigh muscle mass
in the placebo group

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.280
versus virtually none
in the metformin group.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.440
The differences
in strength, however,

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.600
did not reach
statistical significance.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.120
So, might the benefits
of metformin

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.360
outweigh the risks for expanding
the healthspan and lifespan

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.700
of even nondiabetics?

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.560
The investigators
reviewing the evidence

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.560
that diabetics
taking metformin lived longer,

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.140
on average, than nondiabetics,
concluded their

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.880
"results suggest that metformin

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.380
could be an effective
intervention

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:44.940
to extend
the lifespan of people

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.380
who do not have diabetes."

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.900
You can't know, though,

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.720
until you put it to the test,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.540
which I'll explore, next.

